[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Here is a trick that sounds impossible. Take a cheap, fast AI model, the kind you would normally never trust, with a hard architectural decision, and let it borrow the brain of the smartest model'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on Earth, but only for the two or 3 seconds where the decision actually matters. You pay the cheap rate for almost all of the work and the genius rate only for the thinking. Anthropic just shipped this. It is called the'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'adviser tool. and it quietly rewrites the economics of building with AI. By the end of this video, you will understand exactly how it works, when to reach for it, and the settings that'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'decide whether it saves you money or silently burns it. Let me show you. Every team building with AI lives inside the same painful triangle. Fast cheap models like Haiku are wonderful for'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'volume but on a genuinely hard task they will confidently march straight down the wrong path. Big models like Opus make brilliant decisions but running every single step through them is slow and'

[01:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'expensive. So you are forced to choose cheap and occasionally dumb or smart and costly. The advisor tool refuses that choice. It puts two models on one task.'

[01:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'A fast executor that does the bulk of the work and a higher intelligence adviser that the exeutor can quietly consult in the middle of thinking right at the fork in the road. Picture a fast'

[01:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'runner carrying a task down a track. That runner is the exeutor. It is quick, it is cheap, and most of the track is a straight line it can handle on its own.'

[01:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But every so often the track splits and one of the branches is a dead end that the runner cannot see yet. At exactly that fork, the runner stops and calls up'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to an adviser standing high above the track. A slower but far wiser mind that can see the whole map at once. The adviser studies everything the runner'

[02:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'has done so far, hands down a short plan, and the runner sprints on. now heading down the right branch. That is the entire idea. A grandmaster whispering one move into a fast player\'s'

[02:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'ear. Now here is what actually happens inside a single request and it is beautifully simple. You give the fast model your normal tools plus one special tool called adviser. The executive'

[02:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'decides all on its own when the moment is right. And when it calls the adviser, something unusual happens. It sends no input at all. An empty call. Because'

[02:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'behind the scenes, Antropics servers quietly take the entire conversation so far, your instructions, every tool result, everything the model has written this turn and hand that whole transcript'

[03:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to the adviser model. The adviser thinks in private under its own instructions with no tools and nothing to distract it and it sends back a short piece of guidance. Its private'

[03:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'reasoning is thrown away. Only the advice comes back. And here is the part that makes it feel like magic. All of this happens inside one single API call. You do not run two models yourself. You'

[03:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'do not manage a handoff. You send one request to the fast model and somewhere in the middle of writing its answer, it pauses, consults the genius and keeps going all before the response ever lands'

[03:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'back in your hands. From the outside, it looks like one model simply answered. Underneath, two of them collaborated. The fast one did the typing. The smart one made the call that mattered. Let me'

[03:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'show you how little code this actually takes because that is the best part. You are already calling the fast model. Say that is set. You add just one entry to your tools list. Its type is advisor and'

[04:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'inside it you name the model you want as your adviser. Say that is opus. You switch the feature on with a single beta header. And that is it. No new endpoint,'

[04:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'no second client, no glue code. Your fast model now has a genius on speed dial. When it decides to call, you will see a server tool use block with an'

[04:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'empty input followed by an advisor result block carrying the advice. You pass that whole thing back on the next turn exactly like any other message and the conversation just continues. There'

[04:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is one rule you have to respect and it is pure common sense. The adviser has to actually be smarter than or at least as smart as the worker. You cannot have a'

[05:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'genius take orders from a beginner. So the adviser must be Sonnet 4.6 or stronger and never weaker than your executor. The classic pairings are the ones you would guess. If you run Sonnet on hard'

[05:13] [scene:talk]
